    "md5": "ee6d0185691ef7dcf36615c5419551f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1607,
    "chunk_text": "(b) With effect from January 1, 2026, the national minimum monthly wage for all workers in any industry or service shall be thirty thousand rupees, and the national minimum daily wage of a worker shall be one thousand two hundred rupees.\u201d.\n\n3. For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that -\n\nMarch 31, 2025, under the provisions of the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 36 of 2005, the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 4 of 2016, or both, shall form\n\n[Certified on 23rd of July, 2025]\n\nNational Minimum Wage of Workers (Amendment)\n\nAct, No. 11 of 20252\n\npart of the national minimum monthly or daily wage specified in section 2 payable to all workers in any industry or service; and (b) the wage of any worker who, as at March 31,\n\n2025, received a wage that included the budgetary relief allowances under the provisions of the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 36 of 2005, the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 4 of 2016, or both such Acts, shall, from the date of commencement of this Act, consolidate such allowances as part of such wage of such worker.\n\n4. An employer shall not reduce the monthly wage of any worker in any industry or service, including any allowances payable under the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No. 3 of 2016, the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 36 of 2005, or the Budgetary Relief Allowance of Workers Act, No. 4 of 2016, in a manner that would negate the increase made to the national minimum wage by the amendments to the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No. 3 of 2016 under this Act."
