    "chunk_text": "Provided however, nothing in this Act shall, in any manner, prevent or preclude the investigation of offences under the Anti-Corruption Act being conducted in the manner provided for in that Act.\n\nPART I\n\nGeneral Provisions and Offences\n\n(a) the origin, true nature, source, location, disposition, movement, ownership, acquisition, possession, use of, or value of such property or part thereof;\n\n(b) the identities of persons who may have committed the unlawful activity which\n\nApplication of the Act with regard to proceeds of crime derived out of committing offences in the Anti-Corruption Act.\n\nConcealment or disguising of proceeds of crime, etc. to be an offence.\n\nProceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 202510\n\ngave rise to such property; or\n\n(c) the identities of persons who possess beneficial interests relating to such property,\n\ncommits an offence.\n\n7. Any person who knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that a property is proceeds of crime, acquires, possesses, uses, has custody, exercises dominion over, controls, or retains such property commits an offence.\n\n8. Any person who knowingly destroys any evidence relating to any property which is proceeds of crime commits an offence.\n\n9. Any person who breaches or obstructs the enforcement or implementation of any-\n\n(a) restraining order, seizure, judicial freezing\n\norder; (b) notice or order issued by a law enforcement\n\nofficer under this Act;\n\n(c) judicial order issued in respect of an investigation\n\ninto proceeds of crime; or\n\n(d) judicial order made under this Act relating to\n\nproceeds of crime,\n\ncommits an offence.\n\nAcquisition, possession etc. of proceeds of crime to bean offence\n\nBreach or obstruction of the enforcement orimplementation of orders to bean offence.\n\nDestruction. of evidence of proceeds of crime to bean offence.\n\n11Proceeds of Crime Act, No. 5 of 2025\n\n10. Any person served with a notice under section 68 of this Act who-\n\n(a) refuses to accept;\n\n(b) fails to respond truthfully to; or"
